   855 				; Sets 1-3 are pure single-component ramps - set 1 colour i = (i,0,0), set 2 =
   856 				; (0,i,0), set 3 = (0,0,i) - so they are generated straight into the registers
   857 				; rather than stored.  Y walks CR/CG/CB (consecutive registers) for each colour;
   858 				; the component whose register matches the set gets i, the other two get 0.
