  1138 				; it was the separator's boot-time constant fill, but the separator is now a
  1139 				; 160-byte table loaded straight into VRAM (Load_Menu_Sep, init_vbxe.asm), so
  1140 				; this is its only user.  The 12 BCBs already in bcbs.asm exactly fill the
  1141 				; $100-$1FF VBXE VRAM budget (see the memory-map comment at the top of this
  1142 				; file); a 13th BCB overflowed BLT_NFO_NAME_CLEAR across the $200 boundary
  1143 				; into the NTSC_Palette load and corrupted it - do not add a new BCB here.
